			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. [τὸν Ἕκτορα] τῷ τείχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
				</span></i>
			 l.c. :—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Art.</u>
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				352c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1147b16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τοὔνομα</span>
			<i>drag</i> one's good name <i>in the mire</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				7.214d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>divert, distract</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκλῳ π. τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Chrm.</u>
					174b
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. διάνοιαν ἐπί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					6.851
				</span></i>
			 :—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό τινος εἴς τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Longin.
					15.11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
